- [Introduction](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/introduction.md): REST API reference for ScrapeGraphAI v2
- [Error handling](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/errors.md): Error payload shape and HTTP status codes returned by the v2 API
- [Scrape](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/endpoint/scrape.md): Fetch a URL and return its content in one or more formats.
- [Extract](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/endpoint/extract.md): Natural-language structured extraction from a URL, HTML, or markdown.
- [Search](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/endpoint/search.md): Run a web search and fetch the top results in one call.
- [Start crawl](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/endpoint/crawl/start.md): Kick off an async multi-page crawl and return a job id.
- [Get crawl status](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/endpoint/crawl/get-status.md): Poll a running or finished crawl job.
- [Get crawl pages](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/endpoint/crawl/pages.md): Fetch paginated crawl pages with resolved scrape results.
- [Manage crawl jobs](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/endpoint/crawl/manage.md): Stop, resume, and delete running crawl jobs.
- [Create monitor](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/endpoint/monitor/create.md): Schedule a recurring fetch with change detection.
- [Manage monitors](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/endpoint/monitor/manage.md): List, inspect, update, pause, resume, delete monitors and fetch tick activity.
- [History](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/endpoint/history.md): Look up past requests by ID, or list recent requests with optional filters.
- [Credits](https://docs.scrapegraphai.com/api-reference/endpoint/credits.md): Check remaining credits, plan, and job quotas.
